==English==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|fa|صراف|tr=sarâf}} or {{bor|en|ur|صراف|tr=sarrāf}}, from {{der|en|ar|صَرَّاف}}. {{root|en|ar|ص ر ف‎}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ʃɹɒf/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-schroff.wav|Audio (UK)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɒf|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|India}} A [[banker]] or [[moneychanger]].
# {{lb|en|Hong Kong}} A [[cashier]]'s office or [[booth]].
#: {{ux|en|Pay your bill at the '''schroff'''.}}

